Actual gene training input inspection
Date: 2026-04-13 UTC

What the previous log was
- training_data_samples.log contains raw dataset records from CellwText LMDB plus matched caption metadata.
- It is upstream data, not yet the final packed sequence fed into the model.

What the model actually receives for MMUG training
- Dataset output fields: gene_ids, gene_expression, texts
- Prompt builder: training/prompting_utils.py -> mmug_prompt()
- Training callsite: training/train_scmmada.py:835
- Actual packed sequence format before masking is:
  <|mmug|> <|soi|> [gene_tokens] <|eoi|> <bos> [text_tokens] <eos>
- Then prepare_inputs_and_labels_for_mmu(...) applies diffusion masking on the text target side.
- gene_expression is not represented as token ids. It is added later as embedding-level conditioning aligned to the gene token span.

Concrete real sample used below
- Source shard: /data/bgi/data/projects/multimodal/RNA_data/cellwtext_data/CellwText/split_task1_writer1.db
- Sample idx: 0
- cell_id: 607
- raw metadata:
  celltype_name = natural killer cell
  disease_name = normal
  tissue_name = cortex of kidney
  sex_name = male
  stage_name = 38-year-old stage

Actual text condition for this sample
- texts field / caption:
  This cell is a natural killer cell under normal condition from cortex of kidney.

Actual gene side for this sample
- raw gene_ids length in LMDB: 3000
- train config max_gene_tokens: 1200
- real training code first maps LMDB gene ids -> scGPT gene ids, then keeps top 1200 genes by expression, then adds gene_token_offset.
- So the model does NOT receive all 3000 raw gene ids. It receives the top 1200 mapped-and-offset gene tokens.

