Therefore, a readable approximation of the actual MMUG input is
- <|mmug|> <|soi|> [top1200 mapped gene tokens] <|eoi|> <bos> This cell is a natural killer cell under normal condition from cortex of kidney. <eos>

The first few gene tokens conceptually look like
- <|mmug|> <|soi|> [GENE:B2M] [GENE:CCL4] [GENE:MT2A] [GENE:NKG7] [GENE:ACTB] [GENE:BTG1] [GENE:CCL3] [GENE:ACTG1] [GENE:FTL] [GENE:MYL12A] ... <|eoi|> <bos> This cell is a natural killer cell under normal condition from cortex of kidney. <eos>

Important nuance
- The order inside the actual training sequence is expression-sorted top-k after vocab mapping, not the original LMDB order.
- The labels for the gene part are ignore_id in MMUG. The supervised target is the text segment after <|eoi|>.
- Separately, if t2g is enabled, the reverse task packs:
  <|t2g|> <bos> [text_tokens] <eos> <|soi|> [gene_tokens] <|eoi|>
  and only the gene segment is supervised there.

Why I am not showing final text token ids here yet
- I confirmed the exact packing logic from local code.
- I have not confirmed a usable local cache path for the LLaDA tokenizer, so I am not claiming exact text token ids without verifying them.
- If you want, I can keep going and dump one exact input_ids tensor as soon as I locate the tokenizer files on this machine.
